    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0369" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg287"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/629.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-08-06T16:00:00-04:49"><hi rendition="#small-caps">August</hi>
                            6, 1911—4 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>A proclamation dated Gonaives, August 5, proclaiming Leconte chief of the
                    executive power was read in the streets on the morning of the 6th and accepted
                    with calmness. Leconte entered the city at 12.30 with 300 followers and repaired
                    at once to the cathedral for mass. Quiet prevails.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
